      "summary": "Auto-select default IK plating rule when step marked as IK eligible",
      "description": "Background\nPer feedback from Casey: Currently, when a user marks a step as IK eligible in the step-level plating rules UI, when they edit an existing substep, they must perform an additional click to manually select \"default\" as the IK plating rule for sub-steps. This is unnecessary friction.\nRequest\nImplement two automated behaviors when the IK eligible checkbox is toggled:\nIK eligible checkbox from null to true: auto-select \"default\" as the IK plating rule for all sub-steps that currently have a null IK plating rule. Regardless the mapping item/option of the substep is.\nIK eligible checkbox from true to null: auto-clear the IK plating rule for all sub-steps (remove both \"default\" and \"custom\" selections)\nUpdate existing action: \nwhen adding a new substep of which step with IK eligible=true, auto-select  defaul for the IK plating rule. Else, don’t auto-select it.\nWhen create a new line build, don’t default select the 'default' option for IK plating rule.\nReferences\nN/A\nNote / Long-term Direction",
