    {
      "id": "789566",
      "key": "MD-18146",
      "summary": "[Wonder Create] MVP Phase 2: Enable Menu Item Customizations via BYO Model",
      "description": "Background\nIn MVP Phase 1, each menu item created in Wonder Create has a direct 1:1 equivalent in Cookbook with strictly no customizations allowed. Customers cannot remove or swap any ingredient due to personal preference or allergen constraints. Additionally, if a single ingredient goes out of stock, the entire menu item must be marked unavailable, resulting in significant lost sales.\nThis ticket covers MVP Phase 2: leveraging Wonder's existing \nBuild Your Own (BYO)\n architecture (similar to Royal Greens and Yasas) to enable robust customization support for Wonder Create menu items.\nRequest\nFive core requirements from the PRD:\nMaster BYO Template\n — Create a single master BYO Cookbook ID per Wonder Create brand instead of individual 1:1 items.\nSignature Presets Mapping\n — Map each influencer's signature dish as a pre-configured \"preset\" (default selections) on top of the master BYO template.\nScoped BOM Union\n — Dynamically generate the ingredient pool for each brand as the mathematical union of all ingredients across that brand's signature dishes.\nOOS Graceful Degradation\n — When an ingredient is marked out-of-stock, keep the signature preset orderable but prompt the customer to select an alternative ingredient.\nDynamic Pricing Engine\n — Substitutions and extra portions of premium ingredients must be priced dynamically with real-time price and calorie recalculation.\nOpen Questions from PRD:\nQ1: How to determine portion sizes for swaps? (1:1 volumetric/weight replacements, or per-ingredient portion size configuration?)\nQ2: How to determine pricing for swaps? (Credit back the difference, keep a flat base rate, or apply modular pricing based on each protein's default cost?)\nReferences\nPRD: Wonder Create Customizations Support\nNote / Long-term Direction",
