  "metadata": {
    "id": "5125865547",
    "title": "Wonder Create + IK + Cookbook Future State",
    "type": "page",
    "created": "2026-04-16 14:05:24",
    "updated": "2026-04-16 16:09:14",
    "url": "https://wonder.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~712020735951bb19ca4030aef4f98504f0b3da/pages/5125865547",
    "space": {
      "key": "~712020735951bb19ca4030aef4f98504f0b3da",
      "name": "Brandon Galang"
    },
    "author": "Brandon Galang (Deactivated)",
    "version": 4,
    "attachments": [],
    "content": {
      "value": "| Workstream | Status | My Role |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Infinite Kitchens | **Urgent** | IK-eligible data + line build mapping for June pilot |\n| Wonder Create | **In Progress** | Stage 1 API contract with orchestration layer |\n| Future State Cookbook | **Planning / Gated** | W42\\* coordination + UX gated on 41\\* deprecation |\n\n---\n\nInfinite Kitchens\n-----------------\n\nMaintaining IK component ledger and adapting line builds to be human OR IK machine.\n\nDelivering Cookbook-side data changes to support the June pilot: IK-eligible flagging on components and line build updates.\n\n**Open design question:** Cookbook already manages standardized servings (e.g., 50g protein = 1 spoodle of chicken). For IK data pass-through, we need to decide where serving quantity validation lives — human process, HDR product, or Cookbook. Simple to solve, just needs a decision on the right home.\n\nTreating June as a firm target until IK team signals otherwise.\n\n---\n\nWonder Create\n-------------\n\nProviding data endpoints for menu item creation and management for Wonder AI orchestration layer.\n\n**End of Q2 goal:** Cookbook API contract drafted with the Wonder AI orchestration layer (Bart Stein's team).\n\nCookbook owns Stage 1 — receiving the menu item payload and producing BYO line builds with SKU-mapped ingredients. I'm preparing the contract, but holding scope loosely. Pratik is new to Merch ownership and discovery is still early — data management surprises are likely as the orchestration workflow gets defined. Expecting the contract to evolve through Q2.\n\nSeptember Midtown East pilot target.\n\n---\n\nFuture State Cookbook\n---------------------\n\nKeep supporting Supply Chain transition/handoff.\n\nActively avoid coupling and building features meant for supply chain (e.g., SKU shelf life).\n\nRefocus UX around:\n\n1. Menu R&D\n2. Benchtop R&D\n3. Production R&D\n\nSupport platform-level work in Wonder Create.\n\n**Active coordination:**\n\n* Supporting W42\\* transition — collaborating with Sadhana on the frozen/thawed 40\\* item creation workflow as part of the WSKU cutover\n* Aligning on how frozen vs. thawed states propagate through Cookbook's item creation and linking logic\n\n**Gated UX work:**\n\n* Sold status improvements and the difficulty of drilling down from 40\\* to production 88\\* components is blocked by the in-flight 41\\* layer swap/SCC build. No new Cookbook UX features can cleanly ship until that clears.\n\n**Capacity context:**\n\n* ~70% of dev capacity last two months is SCC integration.\n\n**Future state:**\n\n* Post-SCC, Cookbook narrows more cleanly to Menu item R&D and Production R&D, with Fulfillment RCA moving to SCC.\n\n  + Three core flows\n\n    - Create and manage menu items (80\\*)\n    - Create and manage benchtop recipes (3\\*)\n    - Create and manage Wonder-produced SKUs (88\\*s)\n* Cookbook then remains the central platform connector for Production, Consumer App, HDR Portal, Wonder Create/IK, and Inventory.\n\n  + Anticipating Wonder Create could amplify line build + menu item data boundaries issues.",
      "format": "markdown"
    }
  }
}"}

