    "content": {
      "value": "ik--wonder-create-project-discussion-topicsIK & Wonder Create Project Discussion Topics\n=======================================================================================\n\nThis page captures open questions and concerns across two active projects: **IK Potion** and **Wonder Create**. These topics should be aligned with cross-functional stakeholders before implementation begins.\n\n---\n\nik-potionIK Potion\n------------------\n\n### open-questionsOpen Questions\n\n1. Should items fulfilled by IK also be sold at IKC locations that do not have IK equipment?\n2. Should IK-fulfilled items also support manual fulfillment as a fallback?\n3. Should currently live menu items be retrofitted to support IK fulfillment?\n4. Do IK-fulfilled items and non-IK-fulfilled items share the same line build?\n5. If some components marked as **IK Eligible = true** are not loaded in the IK equipment at a given IKC, how should KDS handle those components?\n\n### concernsConcerns\n\n1. **Line build configuration principles are changing.** We are modifying some of CDT's current line build configuration rules to accommodate IK's cooking method. This may cause some existing manually-cooked line builds to become invalid in certain scenarios.\n2. **Dual garnish steps for manual cooking.** To support IK garnish where only IK-eligible components are involved, we need to split the garnish step into two separate steps. When an order is cooked manually (without IK), users will see two garnish steps, which may cause confusion.\n3. **Non-IK cook steps break IK-eligible grouping.** Even after grouping all IK-eligible steps together, they may still be separated by non-IK-eligible cook steps. The current line build convention follows a Cook → Garnish order. See example: [Item 8011818 Line Build](https://cookbook.remarkablefoods.net/ItemV2/detail/line-build/8011818?version_id=2574acc2-71b5-481e-80c7-ab42e093dea3)\n4. **Existing data will fail new validations.** Many current line build entries will not pass the new IK-related validations, requiring CDT to review and update a large number of existing line builds.\n\n---\n\nwonder-createWonder Create\n--------------------------\n\n### customization-supportCustomization Support\n\nOur vision is a **template-style BYO (Build Your Own) item** that defines how each customization should be cooked and how the customization options should be configured. When a user selects certain component items, the system looks up the matching configuration from the template item and assembles the result.\n\n**Required changes in the Orchestration layer:**\n\n1. The API must pass all selected item numbers to Cookbook in a **single request** (rather than one-by-one).\n\n---\n\n### wonder-create-phase-2Wonder Create Phase 2\n\n1. Wonder Create needs to pass **packaged item descriptions** to Cookbook.\n2. **Potion support:** After the IK project finalizes its specification, Cookbook will need to expose each component item's **portion/potion** in the BQ tables. Wonder Create will consume this data to display correct **nutrition information** and **cost** to users.\n3. Per my understanding, we should keep existing BOM data module in Cookbook. That’s saying, Cookbook create wonder create menu item with exactly BOM unit qty instead of portion amount of components. Is there any concern?\n\n   1. Like: 40\\*01 Roasted sweet potato usage is 1 portion in this menu item, and there is ik portion conversion (1 portion=50g) in Cookbook. Then, Cookbook will create menu item 80\\*01 with 40\\*01 Roasted sweet potato x 50g.\n\n      ![image-20260623-101924.png](https://wonder.atlassian.net/wiki/rest/api/content/5400527039/child/attachment/att5400527069/download)\n4. Can IK portion conversion be updated? If yes, once the IK portion conversion of 40\\*01 is updated to 1 portion=28g. Then, what does the portion qty in Wonder Create Portal look like?\n\n   1. It seems weird to show decimal portion, e.g., 50/28=1.785 portion\n5. Configure IK portion conversion at component level in Cookbook\n\n   1. there are many cases which will have the non-integer cases(MD-18122630b433c-e2b3-3fe9-9604-361bca935220System Jira ).\n\n---\n\n### item-name-uniqueness-issueItem Name Uniqueness Issue\n\nTo ensure item names are **unique at the brand level**, we plan to append a brand-scoped unique identifier to Wonder Create item names.\n\n**Impact:**\n\n1. Item names will contain a machine-generated, non-human-readable string suffix.\n2. The item name **character limit will be reduced from 100 → 90** to accommodate the suffix.\n\n---\n\n~~SubStep~~ Task Level Cooking Group\n------------------------------------\n\n1. How does the KDS route via cooking group at substep? there is no appliance/cooking time at substep.\n\n   1. Confirmed by Charlie, should configure at task level rather than substep.\n2. Data: Square Pizza Sauce ([7000075](https://cookbook.remarkablefoods.net/ItemV2/detail/basic/7000075?version_id=70b1318e-b585-4fdb-840a-17a82660b70e)) and Mozzarella Sticks & Marinara, Alanza Pizza ([8011588](https://cookbook.remarkablefoods.net/ItemV2/detail/basic/8011588?version_id=75937938-e2d1-404f-abf9-043bc0e061e8)).\n3. Solution: allow to set cooking group at task\n\n   1. In menu item Mozzarella Sticks & Marinara, Alanza Pizza ([8011588](https://cookbook.remarkablefoods.net/ItemV2/detail/basic/8011588?version_id=75937938-e2d1-404f-abf9-043bc0e061e8)), set mandatory choice customization mapped with Square Pizza Sauce ([7000075](https://cookbook.remarkablefoods.net/ItemV2/detail/basic/7000075?version_id=70b1318e-b585-4fdb-840a-17a82660b70e))\n   2. In the line buld KDS, allow user to set multiple cooking group for a task, regardless the apply to restaurant of the line build is. And regardless the task mapped with customization option or not. Regardless the customization type is.\n   3. KDS rountes the task which mapped with the mandatory choice sauce 7000075 according to the cooking group.\n   4. Note: the above change should be done in both 8011588 and 8010372.\n\n      ![image-20260623-110558.png](https://wonder.atlassian.net/wiki/rest/api/content/5400527039/child/attachment/att5400625450/download)\n\n---\n\nSCC\n===\n\n1. Cook from frozen item list:\n\n   1. double confirm with user whether the below 40\\* should be cooked from frozen. currently, they are in Pantry cook from frozen whitelist. (I think Shin has the knowledge)\n\n      1. ~~4000918. 8807834. Buttermilk Biscuit --whether should be cooked from frozen?~~ It is the cook from frozen pilot\n      2. 4000709. 8807274. Chicken Tender, Fully Cooked Brakebush [Pack, 5LB] FZN-- need menu item list which cook from 40F\n2. Highlight for Scheduled menu item version\n\n   1. <https://remarkable-foods.slack.com/archives/C09JHKH13PF/p1782112679191389>",
