    "content": {
      "value": "Background\n==========\n\n1. We are going to support IK equipment for both current normal menu items and Wonder Create menu items.\n2. IK equipment might have different slot number and module in different HDRs. E,g, Westfield has 10 slots which can support 10 ~~20~~ ingredients. And Quakertown only has 4 slots which can support 4 ~~7~~ ingredients.\n3. The specific IK should have configuration of loaded specific component at HDRs. Then, KDS can understand what components are actually handle by IK at each HDR.\n4. For a component item, it could be cooked in different methods in different menu items. E.g., Chicken cooked by oven in menu item A, it added by IK in menu item B.\n\nProposal\n========\n\n1. Mark specific components as ‘IK Eligible', that’s saying, the **flag is component item level.**\n2. Add new step type “**Activity**= IK step' in line build, and **map all 'IK Eligible' components of the menu item to the sub-steps of the IK step.**\n\n   1. A component is in a IK step only means it is eligible for IK, if it is actually handled by IK or not should also be determined by if the component is loaded in IK or not for this HDR today.\n3. If any IK eligible component should NOT be served by IK at all, CDT can manually remove it from IK step, and configure it to other activity step (e.g, Cook, appliance= turbo oven).\n4. When KDS gets the line builds, KDS should compare the IK eligible components of the IK step against the the actual components loaded in the IK equipment in this specific HDR of today.\n\n   1. If the component is loaded, send to IK. If the component is not loaded, treat it as ‘Garnish’ step to send to the cold pod for manual garnish.\n   2. Note: For a menu item, **as long as the IK eligible components is not served by cook activity step or vend step, CDT configure them in a IK step in a line build in Cookbook.** No need to create different sets of line build for different HDRs where have different IK slot number limited by HDR space.\n\n**Benefits**\n============\n\n1. Reduce manual work for modifying build update\n2. Simplify/easy Line build configuration for CDT\n3. More flexible adjustments for offline operations\n4. Lower risk of inconsistencies between data and cooking processes\n5. Support Wonder Create project\n\n| **Business Scenarios** | **Solution** | **Benifits** |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Change loaded component in IK slots:   * In the beginning, we load **rice**, black bean in IK slots * After a period of time, we load **corn**, black bean | 1. For a menu item with IK eligible components ‘rice’, ‘black bean’, we mapped both of them in IK step in line build. 2. Though the rice slot is changed to corn slot at HDR, KDS can check the IK slots' mapping component from IK, and split rice to an additional garnish step and assign it to cold pod. | 1. No need to change line build if IK loaded component is changed. 2. Operation side could change the slot component in need without waiting for the line build update. |\n| Change loaded component in IK slots:   * The loaded **black bean is OOS** at Westfield HDR, operators can **loads another IK eligible component** (e.g., Red Chili) to IK instead of it **during the service time.** | 1. CDT has mapped all IK eligible components of a menu item to IK step. 2. KDS can check the IK slots' loaded mapping components from IK, and split the un-loaded components to an additional garnish step and assign it to cold pod. | 1. No need to change line build if IK loaded component is changed. 2. Operation side could change the slot component in need without waiting for the line build update. |\n| Different HDRs own different IK slots number:   * Westfield- has 15 IK slots * Chelsea-has 10 IK slots   A menu item with IK eligible components (e.g., 12 components), Westfield has IK slots for all of them, Chelsea only only has 10 components. | KDS can check the IK slots' mapping component from IK in Chelsea, and split the components to an additional garnish step and assign it to cold pod. | 1. No need to build multiple sets of line build via HDRs. 2. And the IK slots' loaded components can be flexible changed in need. 3. CDT no need to understand what IK components in specific HDR while line build configuration. |\n| Wonder Create project   * The Influencer free to create menu items via AI creator. * No manual review on line build * Influencer can update created menu item component and no CE review action on the line build. | 1. Cookbook auto-generate line build for the wonder create menu item.     1. Aggregate all the IK eligible components of the menu item to IK step in line build.    2. And mark the other non-IK eligible components to garnish step in the line build.    3. **NOTE: we don’t support other cooking steps (e.g., cook in oven).** 2. When influencer updates the created menu item component.     1. Cookbook auto-update the IK/garnish step of the line build. | 1. More flexible for wonder create project and don’t the consider the IK loaded components in HDRs. |\n\nConfiguration Sample\n====================\n\nBackground\n----------\n\n* IK Eligible=**true** components\n\n  + 40\\*01 Bean, Black, Canned, Low Sodium, [Drained] HC\n  + 40\\*02 Pinto Beans (HDR Retail) HC\n  + 70\\*01 White Rice (Cooked) [Rice Cooker, 21x]\n  + 70&02 Brown Rice (Cooked) [Rice Cooker, 21x]\n  + 40\\*03 Corn Salsa\n  + 40\\*04 Salsa Verde\n  + 40\\*05 Salsa, Red Chili (Buyout) HC\n\nIK Eligible=**false** components\n\n* 70\\*03 Diced Adobo Chicken Thighs [Cooked, 3x]\n\n| **#** | **Menu Item Configuration** | **Line build** | **Operation case** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Case 1:  BOM line item case | Menu item: Chicken Bowl, Salad has the below components in BOM:   * 70\\*03 Diced Adobo Chicken Thighs [Cooked, 3x] **(NOT IK Eligible)** * 40\\*01 Bean, Black, Canned, Low Sodium, [Drained] HC **(IK Eligible=true)** * 70\\*01 White Rice (Cooked) [Rice Cooker, 21x] **(IK Eligible=true)** * 40\\*03 Corn Salsa **(IK Eligible=true)** * 40\\*04 Salsa Verde **(IK Eligible=true)** * 40\\*05 Salsa, Red Chili (Buyout) HC **(IK Eligible=true)** | **Line Build configuration: Apply to all restaurant**  Step 1: Activity=Cook, Appliance=oven   * Sub-step mapping item: 70\\*03 Diced Adobo Chicken Thighs [Cooked, 3x], Ingredient/Step Title: cook chicken   Step 2: Activity= IK Step   * Sub-step mapping item: 40\\*01 Bean, Black, Canned, Low Sodium, [Drained] HC **(IK Eligible=true)** * Sub-step mapping item: 70\\*01 White Rice (Cooked) [Rice Cooker, 21x] **(IK Eligible=true)** * Sub-step mapping item: 40\\*03 Corn Salsa **(IK Eligible=true)** * Sub-step mapping item: 40\\*04 Salsa Verde **(IK Eligible=true)** * Sub-step mapping item: 40\\*05 Salsa, Red Chili (Buyout) HC **(IK Eligible=true)**   Step 3: Activity=Complete   * Sub-step mapping item: 90\\*01, Ingredient/Step Title: Place in Large Bag, Parking Spot: Warm | 1. If Westfield HDR IK slots have components: Black Bean, Pinto Beans, White Rice, Brown Rice, Corn Salsa, Tomatillo Salsa (Medium), Red Chile Salsa (Medium). 2. And Quakertown HDR only has black bean, Corn Salsa. 3. Then when customer place order with the menu item in Quakertown HDR, **KDS split the components ‘White Rice’, ‘Salsa Verde’ and ‘Salsa, Red Chili (Buyout) HC’ to garnish step and push it to cold pod.** 4. For the IK Step, if the sticky dupe needs to show the component name, we can auto-capture the OOS name of the component to the Ingredient/Step Title of the sub-step.     1. The OOS name is the name to display on Wonder App if this component item is non-integal and it is OOS. |\n| Case 2:  Customization case | Menu item: Bowl (BYO), Lime salt has the below customizations:  **Choose your protein:**   * Chicken: 70\\*03 Diced Adobo Chicken Thighs [Cooked, 3x] **(NOT IK Eligible)** * Steak: 40\\*06 Adobo Steak (Fabricated) HC **(NOT IK Eligible)**   **Choose your bean:**   * Bean, Black: 40\\*01 Bean, Black, Canned, Low Sodium, [Drained] HC **(IK Eligible=true)** * Pinto Beans: 40\\*02 Pinto Beans (HDR Retail) HC **(IK Eligible=true)**   **Choose your rice:**   * White Rice: 70\\*01 White Rice (Cooked) [Rice Cooker, 21x] **(IK Eligible=true)** * Brown Rice: 70&02 Brown Rice (Cooked) [Rice Cooker, 21x] **(IK Eligible=true)**   **Choose your toppings:**   * Corn Salsa: 40\\*03 Corn Salsa **(IK Eligible=true)** * Tomatillo Salsa (Medium): 40\\*04 Salsa Verde **(IK Eligible=true)** * Red Chile Salsa (Medium): 40\\*05 Salsa, Red Chili (Buyout) HC **(IK Eligible=true)** | **Line Build configuration: Apply to all restaurant**  Step 1: Cook- turbo oven   * sub step: map customization option: Chicken, Ingredient/Step Title: cook chicken   Step 2: Cook-turbo oven   * sub step: map customization option: Steak, Ingredient/Step Title: cook steak   Step 3: IK step   * sub step: map customization option: Bean, Black * sub step: map customization option: Pinto Beans * sub step: map customization option: White Rice * sub step: map customization option: Brown Rice * sub step: map customization option: Corn Salsa * sub step: map customization option: Tomatillo Salsa (Medium) * sub step: map customization option: Red Chile Salsa (Medium)   Step 3: Activity=Complete   * Sub-step mapping item: 90\\*01, Ingredient/Step Title: Place in Large Bag, Parking Spot: Warm | 1. For the IK step mapped with customization option, Cookbook reply both mapping customization option and its related mapping item to KDS. |",
      "format": "markdown"
    },
