    "content": {
      "value": "**Status:** Draft — pending engineering input  \n**Next step:** Share with Cookbook eng and Wonder Create eng for implementation alignment\n\n---\n\nContext\n-------\n\nWonder Create is an AI-assisted platform for external creators to design and publish restaurants on Wonder. The AI generates a restaurant concept — name, description, and menu items — from a creator prompt. Each menu item is composed from Wonder's approved consumable items.\n\n**Current state relevant to this integration:**\n\n* Creators select consumable items to compose their menu items. There are no customer-facing customizations in scope for MVP.\n* Wonder Create currently works from a CSV export of IK-supported consumables. This list is not actively synced from Cookbook.\n* Before anything publishes, a Wonder-side human reviewer approves the concept.\n* Once approved, Wonder Create needs to create the corresponding items in Wonder's systems and get stable IDs back. Those IDs are required for any future edits.\n\n---\n\nProblem\n-------\n\nWonder Create has no defined contract for handing off approved AI-generated menu items to Cookbook. Without it:\n\n* The consumable list Wonder Create works from drifts from what Cookbook actually supports\n* There is no stable ID to reference when a creator edits their menu item post-publish\n* Wonder Create is forced to manage Cookbook-internal complexity it should not own\n\n---\n\nFunctional Requirements\n-----------------------\n\n### F1 — Wonder Create can retrieve an approved list of consumable items\n\nCookbook owns and maintains the list of consumable items (40\\*) approved for Wonder Create use. Wonder Create uses this list to constrain what creators can select when composing menu items.\n\n* Each entry includes a stable Cookbook item ID and a display name\n* UOM is defined by the item record itself; nutrition is calculated from item records — Wonder Create does not supply either\n* CE / chefs maintain this list in Cookbook\n* Wonder Create pulls and caches it; real-time sync not required for MVP\n\n**How the list is maintained:**  \nWonder Create is currently prototyping off a CSV export of IK-supported consumables.\n\nWe can transition this to a Cookbook owned List (perhaps our existing List objects with an API) or a new Wonder Create specific structure if they need additional organization and structure.\n\n---\n\n### F2 — Wonder Create can create a menu item in Cookbook and receive a stable item ID\n\nAt publish (after human review passes), Wonder Create sends each menu item to Cookbook. Cookbook creates the records and returns a stable item ID.\n\n**Wonder Create sends:**\n\n* Item name\n* BOM: list of consumable item IDs (40\\*) with quantities\n* Line build: authored by Wonder Create using Cookbook/CE-provided templates per item type\n\n**Cookbook returns:**\n\n* A stable `item_id` that Wonder Create stores for future updates\n* Exact failure messages if creation fails\n\n---\n\n### F3 — Wonder Create can update a previously created menu item using its item ID\n\nCreators can edit their restaurant after initial publish. Wonder Create uses the `item_id` from F2 to push changes.\n\n**What is editable via this API:**\n\n| Field | Editable | Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Item name | Yes | Wonder Create owns display names |\n| BOM — which consumables | Yes | Swap in/out 40\\* items |\n| BOM — quantities | Yes | Adjust per consumable |\n| Line build | Yes | Re-submit updated steps |\n| Customizations (modifier groups, optional add/remove) | No | Out of scope for MVP |\n\nSame validation runs as create; exact failure messages on failure.\n\n---\n\nPrerequisite\n------------\n\nCE must define and maintain line build templates and rules per item type before Wonder Create can author line builds. This will effectively mirror how we handle Preset items with the parent BYO item having the superset line build with all potential steps.\n\nIn the future, we may use our Cookbook agent + line build tools to author line builds just-in-time.\n\n---\n\nOpen Questions for Engineering\n------------------------------\n\nWhat is the line build submission format — what exactly does Wonder Create send?\n\n> Jakob: cookbook should define the data model, to define this we should be very clear about the ability of IK. like i comment above in `Prerequisite`\n\nHow should Cookbook expose the approved consumable list?\n\n> Jakob: @Brandon Galang (Deactivated) can you be more specific about this question?\n>\n> As far as I know, we should maintain a list of ingredient list, this list could be from existing menu items‘s consumable items + some more user manually identified consumable items. and we expose the list as an API.\n>\n> Bonnie: @Brandon Galang (Deactivated) After CE reviews the ingredient list, we can tag a flag (e.g., Wonder Create Item), any item (non-dormant and published) with the flag can be exposed to Wonder Creator. If any new ingredient should expose to Wonder creator, CE can tag the flag in need.\n>\n> If any ingredient is not for service any more, CE needs to swap it with a new one or remove it from all existing Wonder Create menu items. Then, dormant the deprecated ingredient or remove the flag.\n\nIs it creating one atomic call (item + BOM + line build together) or sequenced?\n\nJakob:\n\n> cc @Bob Weibin this is a big topic, not only bom + linebuild, but also brand, restaurant, concept, merch brand item, merch menu all together. Seeing from the figma it’s just a `publish` button, and a lot of validations should be done with one single click.\n>\n> We still under discussion with the\n>\n> I am not super concern with cookbook domain including (brand, concept, BOM, line build) in cookbook we should expose as a atomic call, because all of the business are within the cookbook domain. As long as we have a clear scope and integrate with IK this is not a difficult part.\n>\n> Here is a high level brief sequence that we need to do:\n>\n> to publish a sellable menu item crossing HDR, Cookbook and Merch\n>\n> 1. HDR\n>\n>    1. setup the IK as a new pod(one time setup)\n>\n> After we click `publish` we should do following works:\n>\n> 2. cookbook\n>\n>    1. need to create concept\n>    2. create brand\n>    3. create menu item\n>    4. create line build\n> 3. merch\n>\n>    1. create brand menu item\n>    2. create menu based on the list of HDRs that supporting IK\n>    3. add menu item into menu\n>    4. publish the menu\n>\n> After all all the menu items can be sold in wonder app.\n\nWhat are the update semantics — full replace or partial patch?\n\nJakob:\n\n> partial patch in cookbook, but for wonder create, they should send ID + updated semantics.\n\nOpen questions from Engineering team\n------------------------------------\n\nRegarding the validation, are AI team going to call cookbook APIs just like AI Agent do?\n\n> 1. AI team call based on cookbook API define\n> 2. Cookbook return failed reason\n> 3. AI Agent resolve the issue and call again\n>\n> Another option is to define a validation rule beforehand, and the Wonder Create UI will only output correct data.\n\nKnowing from @Charlie Fox, KDS only needs a list of ingredients, and IK could arrange the cooking phase. May the cookbook need to define the packaging, finishing, and labeling steps?\n\nWhat if cookbook ingredient is no longer available for any reason? @Bonnie Baohuan",
      "format": "markdown"
    }
