  "summary": "[WC] Auto Assign Packaging for WC Menu Item",
  "description": "## Background\nWonder Create Portal currently passes item creation requests to Cookbook but does not include packaging type information. Cookbook defaults all WC items to a standard bowl, which breaks kitchen execution for dishes with multiple leafy greens or high total weight — those need larger containers (48oz or large bowl) to be physically executable.\n## Request\n1. If item type=bowl/salad, packaging default to bowl, and influencer should choose the packaging type.\n![\"image-20260605-075724.png\"](image-20260605-075724.png)\n1. Wonder Create AI generates the images for packaging (e.g., bowl or foil paper) shown in WC portal.\n1. Cookbook no need to provide 9\\* item list to Wonder Create Portal.\n1. Wonder Create portal no need to provide 9\\* item number to Orchestration Layer.\n1. Influencer needs to select ‘item type’, and Cookbook could identify the packaging type from the item type value.\n1. If item type= bowls, use:\n1. For 48 oz bowl, use: 9000041 Bowl, 48oz, Natural, Round, Pulp  9001727 Lid, 32 & 48oz Pulp Bowl, PET, Dome\n1. For 32 oz bowl, use: 9000061 Bowl, 32oz, Natural, Round, Pulp  9001727 Lid, 32 & 48oz Pulp Bowl, PET, Dome\n1. If item type=wrap, use:\n- 9000260 Sheet, 14x16\", Foil, Insulated, Honeycomb\n1. CDT will tag attribute 'Component Type=Green' on wonder create component items, which uses for the selection of bowl size.\n1. Cookbook should auto-select the correct packaging item (9\\*) in wonder create menu item creation based on:\n- Either if the total portions of component items with green attribute >= 2, select 48oz bowl\n- Or if total food weight of components exceeds threshold 32oz, select 48 oz bowl\n1. Auto-tag IK dish type and IK plating rule attribute on wonder create menu item \\*\\*(updated by Bonnie: 6/11)\\*\\*\n1. When creating/updating wonder create menu item, update the IK dish type and IK plating rule attribute if item type/non-food item is changed.\n1. The menu item should use default IK dish type and IK plating rule attribute in line build. \\*\\*(updated by Bonnie: 6/11)\\*\\*\n1. The way of identify the dish type/plating rule for a wonder create item\\*\\*(updated by Bonnie: 6/11)\\*\\*\n1. if a wonder create menu item with item type= bowls, and its 9\\* item is 48oz bowl, then the IK dish type attribute=48oz Bowl, IK plating rule=LAYERING\n1. if a wonder create menu item with item type= bowls, and its 9\\* item is 32oz bowl, then the IK dish type attribute=32oz Bowl, IK plating rule=LAYERING\n1. if a wonder create menu item with item type=wrap, then the IK dish type attribute=Metal Bowl, IK Plating Rule=CENTER\n1. Data migration:\n1. Initial attribute 'Component Type=Green' on existing wonder create component items according to the green component list for inifialization.\n1. Note: according to conversation in comments:\n1. Cookbook provide the 9\\* list to Wonder Create.\n1. Wonder Create portal no need to provide 9\\*\\* item number to Orchestration Layer. Thus, if wonder create portal return the 9\\*\\* item to Orchestration layer, Cookbook will ignore the 9\\*.",
