on which is no mapping item, IK plating rule is optional. (implement in [MD-17978](https://wonder.atlassian.net/browse/MD-17978))\n  1. IK Eligible flag toggle true →  false: Previously set plating rules on sub-steps are preserved (not auto-cleared)\n1. Show configurations in line build list.\n  1. Show default attributes underneath 'Apply Restaurants'\n  1. For custom sub-step, show 'IK Plating Rules' \n![\"image-20260513-090239.png\"](image-20260513-090239.png)\n1. Add the 'IK Plating Rules' of line build to change log.\n1. API support: \n  1. Please return the 'IK Dish Type' of the menu item,and the IK plating rule of sub-steps to KDS\n  1. If the sub-step doesn’t designate the custom IK plating rule, please return the 'IK Plating Rules' attribute of the menu item to KDS. Else, return the designated custom IK plating rule to KDS.\n1. Once the IK plating rule attribute of the menu item is change, the default plating rule of sub-step in line build should be auto-updated.\n1. Once the IK plating rule attribute of the menu item is removed, the default plating rule value of sub-step in line build should be null. And user needs to unselect the checked ‘Default’ option by manual before saving the line build.\n1. Currently, the line build/attributes configurations of preset item is synced from BYO menu item. We will keep this logic.\n  1. That’s saying, if the BYO item with ‘IK Dish Type=48 oz bowl’, then all its preset items will be ‘IK Dish Type=48 oz bowl’ as well.\n  1. The ‘IK Plating Rules’ attribute on the BYO menu item and its override ‘IK Plating Rules’ on sub-step, which will be synced to all its preset items.\n1. API:\n  1. We should return the ‘IK Plating Rules’ via sub-step.\n  1. The 'IK Dish Type' should be return at line build level.\n  1. Regardless of the 'IK eligible' flag is, Cookbook returns whatever configuration exist in line build to KDS. And whether the value is consumed in KDS should determined by 'IK eligible' flag. [https://remarkable-foods.sl